WEBVTT

00:00:19.370 --> 00:00:20.410
Huh?

00:00:20.410 --> 00:00:22.370
Hey, it's been a while.

00:00:22.370 --> 00:00:23.870
I say that every time.

00:00:23.870 --> 00:00:25.000
Ah!

00:00:25.000 --> 00:00:25.870
Huh?

00:00:25.870 --> 00:00:28.580
You look pale. What's the matter?

00:00:28.580 --> 00:00:30.450
Oh, that?

00:00:30.450 --> 00:00:33.540
I mentioned that it was
my birthday earlier today,

00:00:33.540 --> 00:00:41.620
so Mr. Mato got a cake for me to celebrate a
little since I'll be working until 4 AM tonight.

00:00:41.620 --> 00:00:43.200
Ah, Miss Minare. Did you--?

00:00:43.200 --> 00:00:46.830
I wanted to celebrate with you,
but someone beat me to it!

00:00:46.830 --> 00:00:50.160
It feels especially painful for me right now.

00:00:50.160 --> 00:00:51.620
Tell me... why?

00:00:51.620 --> 00:00:55.000
I busted my butt over here.

00:00:55.000 --> 00:00:57.910
But I was still outdone by someone... Why?

00:00:57.910 --> 00:00:59.160
Miss Minare!

00:00:59.160 --> 00:01:03.330
I've celebrated my birthday
at work before a few times,

00:01:03.330 --> 00:01:06.870
but this is the first time I've
celebrated twice in one day!

00:01:06.870 --> 00:01:10.330
Right now I'm so happy.
I can't believe this is happening.

00:01:10.330 --> 00:01:12.200
Thank you so much!

00:01:13.330 --> 00:01:15.580
Mizuho...

00:01:15.580 --> 00:01:17.450
Miss Minare...

00:01:17.450 --> 00:01:19.160
I wanna make love to you.

00:01:20.040 --> 00:01:22.250
Let's have our meeting, shall we?

00:01:22.250 --> 00:01:25.290
I beg you please, give us
ten minutes to celebrate.

00:01:25.290 --> 00:01:27.290
Sorry, we don't have that kind of time.

00:01:28.500 --> 00:01:31.830
So... Did you think of a good segment idea?

00:01:31.830 --> 00:01:33.660
"*Minare whined about it so she was given ten
minutes to celebrate before the meeting."
Actually... I've got nothing...

00:01:33.660 --> 00:01:34.910
"*Minare whined about it so she was given ten
minutes to celebrate before the meeting."

00:01:34.910 --> 00:01:36.950
"*Minare whined about it so she was given ten
minutes to celebrate before the meeting."
You gotta be kidding me.

00:03:07.660 --> 00:03:10.450
"Episode 5: You're Not Getting Out Alive"
This program has your name in the title.

00:03:10.450 --> 00:03:13.870
"Episode 5: You're Not Getting Out Alive"
But all you're going to do is open
your mouth and wait to be fed.

00:03:15.700 --> 00:03:17.040
Ah...

00:03:17.040 --> 00:03:19.200
He's scarier than usual.

00:03:21.660 --> 00:03:23.120
That's a good one.

00:03:23.120 --> 00:03:24.700
All right, let's go with that.

00:03:24.700 --> 00:03:27.750
Wait, I didn't say anything.
You're weirding me out.

00:03:28.580 --> 00:03:29.450
My bad.

00:03:29.450 --> 00:03:34.910
I had already decided that this would be
an irregular program that has no fixed format.

00:03:34.910 --> 00:03:38.790
It's all going to be based on
spontaneous ideas and random content.

00:03:38.790 --> 00:03:40.330
Random content...?

00:03:40.330 --> 00:03:42.950
This is tonight's script and cue sheet.

00:03:42.950 --> 00:03:44.120
Okay...

00:03:44.120 --> 00:03:46.450
The script is written by Kureko.

00:03:46.450 --> 00:03:48.700
Remember the first time you were here?

00:03:48.700 --> 00:03:52.290
He's the old guy who was
in the booth with Chishiro.

00:03:52.290 --> 00:03:55.500
The first episode is going to be
a fictitious report.

00:03:55.500 --> 00:03:58.700
Huh? What exactly is a fictitious report?

00:03:58.700 --> 00:04:01.950
"Fictitious Report"
It's exactly as it sounds.
It's a fictitious happening.

00:04:01.950 --> 00:04:05.540
"Fictitious Report"
It's a style of radio drama
that sounds like a report.

00:04:05.540 --> 00:04:07.500
It's like "The War of the Worlds."

00:04:07.500 --> 00:04:11.580
Back in the day, Orson Welles reported
breaking news of a Martian invasion

00:04:11.580 --> 00:04:14.160
in the middle of a music program on the radio.

00:04:14.160 --> 00:04:17.700
It was actually a radio drama adaptation
of <i>The War of the Worlds</i>,

00:04:17.700 --> 00:04:21.580
but it caused panic among
the listeners who believed it was real.

00:04:21.580 --> 00:04:24.080
It's a bit of an urban legend now...

00:04:24.080 --> 00:04:26.330
The reporter for today's episode

00:04:26.330 --> 00:04:30.750
is a woman who just murdered the man
who betrayed her and ran away.

00:04:30.750 --> 00:04:32.450
What kind of scenario is that?

00:04:32.450 --> 00:04:35.500
The program will air at 3:32 AM.

00:04:35.500 --> 00:04:39.410
We'll cut off Sound High Tide after the first
two minutes and start without any introduction.

00:04:39.410 --> 00:04:43.040
There won't be any mention of
the program title, sponsors, or ads.

00:04:43.040 --> 00:04:46.700
It'll end abruptly and go right back
into Sound High Tide.

00:04:46.700 --> 00:04:49.790
We're going to put on a fake broadcast gaffe.

00:04:49.790 --> 00:04:52.790
As if someone hijacked the radio waves.

00:04:52.790 --> 00:04:57.620
Well, listeners these days are jaded,
so they'll most likely realize it's scripted.

00:04:57.620 --> 00:05:00.370
But if it can creep people out
for a second, I'll be happy.

00:05:00.370 --> 00:05:04.200
Wait a minute. Not mentioning
the title or ads is already bad enough,

00:05:04.200 --> 00:05:06.950
but not mentioning the sponsor?
That's not going to fly.

00:05:06.950 --> 00:05:10.580
Minare, there won't be any
sponsors for this program.

00:05:10.580 --> 00:05:11.620
What?!

00:05:11.620 --> 00:05:16.330
It's a non-sponsored slot that
the radio station covers the cost for.

00:05:16.330 --> 00:05:21.040
Typically, they air the news in this slot.

00:05:21.040 --> 00:05:26.830
Since there's no sponsor, there's more freedom
when it comes to the content you air.

00:05:26.830 --> 00:05:30.870
"*Image of convincing tactics"
The reason it took this long to get back to you
wasn't because we were looking for sponsors.

00:05:30.870 --> 00:05:32.540
"*Image of convincing tactics"
It just took time to convince the higher-ups.

00:05:32.950 --> 00:05:35.910
This slot is usually hosted by one
of our regular radio announcers,

00:05:35.910 --> 00:05:38.660
so there's no extra appearance fees.

00:05:38.660 --> 00:05:40.660
Well of course!

00:05:40.660 --> 00:05:42.290
Oh... Give me a break.

00:05:42.290 --> 00:05:47.160
Since there's no sponsor to worry about,
we can take it easy, which is nice.

00:05:47.160 --> 00:05:50.660
You don't have to worry about the numbers.

00:05:50.660 --> 00:05:53.040
This is all my doing.

00:05:53.040 --> 00:05:57.830
Should this program fail,
you have the curry shop to fall back on.

00:05:57.830 --> 00:05:58.660
Isn't that right?

00:05:58.660 --> 00:06:01.660
I told him I'm about to get fired there.

00:06:01.660 --> 00:06:02.580
Minare.

00:06:02.580 --> 00:06:03.870
Huh?

00:06:03.870 --> 00:06:06.580
Take Madoka Chishiro as an example.
She's a personality

00:06:06.580 --> 00:06:09.290
who's good at keeping things moving
and selecting songs to play.

00:06:09.290 --> 00:06:13.160
She's able to respond to listeners with
levelheaded, compassionate comments,

00:06:13.160 --> 00:06:15.250
which they want to hear.

00:06:15.250 --> 00:06:22.410
We could train you as a versatile personality
or DJ like her, which you could be someday,

00:06:22.410 --> 00:06:24.040
but what good would that be?

00:06:24.040 --> 00:06:26.910
I'd probably be able to make a living.

00:06:26.910 --> 00:06:32.580
I just want to play around a little
using your voice as my new toy.

00:06:32.580 --> 00:06:35.080
"Impending sense of doom"
Impending sense of doom...

00:06:35.580 --> 00:06:39.290
What's with this script?
There're too many ad-lib sections!

00:06:39.290 --> 00:06:40.950
What's the point of having a writer?

00:06:40.950 --> 00:06:44.290
Just go with it. We're on in five minutes.

00:06:45.290 --> 00:06:48.750
Did something happen before this?

00:06:48.750 --> 00:06:49.870
Why do you ask?

00:06:49.870 --> 00:06:53.410
Today's your official radio debut.

00:06:53.410 --> 00:06:57.040
Thought you'd be a bit more excited than this.

00:06:58.330 --> 00:07:01.620
Yeah, tell me about it.

00:07:01.620 --> 00:07:05.000
Mr. Mato, tell me something good about myself.

00:07:05.000 --> 00:07:09.160
What? Is that something you ask someone
you've only known a few months?

00:07:09.160 --> 00:07:12.660
--Well... You're quick-witted
with a distinct and clear voice.

00:07:12.660 --> 00:07:13.950
--Well, yeah.
--Well... You're quick-witted
with a distinct and clear voice.

00:07:13.950 --> 00:07:18.330
Of course you'd say that, Mr. Mato.

00:07:18.330 --> 00:07:20.910
But what do you think of me as a woman?

00:07:22.500 --> 00:07:27.200
Honestly, you'd attract more guys
if you just stood there in silence.

00:07:27.200 --> 00:07:32.910
What? That means if I continue working with you,
Mr. Mato, my luck with men will only dwindle!

00:07:34.120 --> 00:07:37.950
You might be right...
Since I want to keep you to myself.

00:07:37.950 --> 00:07:39.290
That's the idea.

00:07:40.290 --> 00:07:42.120
Miss Minare, you're on in one minute.

00:07:42.120 --> 00:07:47.000
All right! My baseless self-confidence
has come back just in time!

00:07:47.000 --> 00:07:47.950
Minare.

00:07:47.950 --> 00:07:50.620
You're a curry restaurant worker
who's about to broadcast

00:07:50.620 --> 00:07:52.500
a dead-of-night one-person show at 3 AM

00:07:52.500 --> 00:07:55.120
via seven relay stations without
even mentioning the title.

00:07:55.120 --> 00:07:55.950
--It's not even on the schedule.
Everything about it is irregular.

00:07:55.950 --> 00:07:58.580
--Ten seconds...
--It's not even on the schedule.
Everything about it is irregular.

00:07:58.580 --> 00:08:01.660
Everything depends on the listeners'
comments on the web.

00:08:01.660 --> 00:08:03.830
--Four... Three...
--Give them something to talk about.

00:08:03.830 --> 00:08:04.910
Two...

00:08:04.910 --> 00:08:06.040
One...

00:08:06.040 --> 00:08:07.250
Go!

00:08:12.830 --> 00:08:15.370
You deserve this.

00:08:15.370 --> 00:08:16.790
Mitsuo...

00:08:18.410 --> 00:08:22.700
All that passionate sweet talk
doesn't cost you a dime.

00:08:22.700 --> 00:08:28.700
After all, for you women are
just easy money... Am I wrong?

00:08:28.700 --> 00:08:34.950
That nature of yours... It won't be fixed
until you die and reincarnate.

00:08:34.950 --> 00:08:37.500
Right, Mitsuo?

00:08:44.250 --> 00:08:46.830
"3:30 Sound High Tide"

00:08:46.830 --> 00:08:51.500
I did it! I finally did it.
I finally killed Mitsuo!

00:08:56.200 --> 00:08:59.500
Stabbing someone was scary...

00:08:59.500 --> 00:09:03.410
It's been a while since I got this scared...

00:09:03.410 --> 00:09:06.200
Not since I pierced my ears...

00:09:07.580 --> 00:09:11.080
"Unstable breathing throughout the lines.
(Ad-lib laughs here and there.)"
But this heaviness of heart
doesn't compare with the time

00:09:11.080 --> 00:09:13.580
I had to take Elvis to the animal hospital.

00:09:13.580 --> 00:09:16.250
There's no need to keep
a stable distance with the mic.

00:09:16.250 --> 00:09:20.080
Unstable acoustic pressure makes it
sound more convincing as a gaffe.

00:09:20.080 --> 00:09:22.830
"Talk about the story for about a minute.
Good luck."
Yes... It was my third year in junior high...

00:09:22.830 --> 00:09:24.580
"Talk about the story for about a minute.
Good luck."
I stopped at the bookstore
while I was on a walk.

00:09:24.580 --> 00:09:27.330
I really regret doing that...

00:09:27.330 --> 00:09:30.000
I was reading a book for 30 minutes
holding on to the leash.

00:09:30.000 --> 00:09:32.540
Elvis fell asleep by my feet.

00:09:32.540 --> 00:09:35.540
A group of grannies were
gossiping right next to us.

00:09:35.540 --> 00:09:40.200
Then, one of the grannies tripped over
laughing and stepped on the leash.

00:09:40.200 --> 00:09:46.040
Come on, what did you expect? Of course the
startled dog would bite you. It makes sense!

00:09:46.040 --> 00:09:48.330
--Why didn't I just go straight home?

00:09:48.330 --> 00:09:49.950
--That's horrible...
--Why didn't I just go straight home?

00:09:49.950 --> 00:09:57.450
Compared to that time, I don't feel an ounce of
compassion or pity towards this piece of trash.

00:09:57.450 --> 00:10:04.500
Sadness and guilt only arise if there is some
kind of irrationality surrounding the death.

00:10:04.500 --> 00:10:08.620
But when you kill someone
who deserves to be killed...

00:10:08.620 --> 00:10:14.620
There's no guilt. I cleaned up the trash
and isolated the entropy.

00:10:14.620 --> 00:10:17.160
Now I feel hollow inside...

00:10:17.160 --> 00:10:20.410
"You're annoyed about killing some worthless guy
so you try to list a few good things about him."
Now I feel hollow inside...

00:10:21.910 --> 00:10:24.540
--What... is this...?
--Going to prison for killing some boring guy?
That would be unbearable.

00:10:24.540 --> 00:10:26.290
--What?
--Going to prison for killing some boring guy?
That would be unbearable.

00:10:26.290 --> 00:10:30.330
Let's look back on the few
good points about him...

00:10:30.330 --> 00:10:35.250
When it came to my appearance,
he was the first to notice.

00:10:35.250 --> 00:10:38.580
"Those earrings are new,
aren't they? They're cute."

00:10:38.580 --> 00:10:41.950
He was skilled at complimenting girls like that.

00:10:41.950 --> 00:10:44.120
Even though he's a Kyushu man.

00:10:44.120 --> 00:10:49.950
But maybe that moocher constitution
was something he was born with.

00:10:49.950 --> 00:10:54.200
Now that would be cruel, if that were the case.

00:10:54.200 --> 00:10:56.120
Here I am dissing him after all.

00:10:56.120 --> 00:10:59.870
But who cares. "Dead men tell no tales," right?

00:10:59.870 --> 00:11:04.540
Whenever we ate out, it always ended up
being me paying or splitting the check.

00:11:04.540 --> 00:11:08.700
The way he said, "I'm getting hungry" was cute.

00:11:08.700 --> 00:11:11.330
Cute? What the heck am I saying?

00:11:11.330 --> 00:11:14.330
I'm so pathetic, aren't I...?

00:11:16.000 --> 00:11:20.700
Ah, well... Mitsuo's dead now.

00:11:20.700 --> 00:11:25.580
I didn't expect the knife
to pierce through so easily.

00:11:25.580 --> 00:11:31.830
--But it makes sense... Your stomach's
not a lump of meat, it's a hollow tube.

00:11:31.830 --> 00:11:34.160
--This voice...
--But it makes sense... Your stomach's
not a lump of meat, it's a hollow tube.

00:11:34.160 --> 00:11:37.290
Of course I didn't mean to kill him.

00:11:37.290 --> 00:11:40.040
Over a mere 500,000 yen?

00:11:40.040 --> 00:11:43.080
It wasn't like I hated him, either.

00:11:43.080 --> 00:11:47.370
I just wanted him to turn over a new leaf.

00:11:49.950 --> 00:11:52.660
What the hell is this?

00:11:54.200 --> 00:11:57.000
Whoa, that's bright... Is that a car?

00:11:57.000 --> 00:12:01.330
They're here already, huh? Well, that was fast.

00:12:01.330 --> 00:12:05.830
When I get out, I'll become a better woman.

00:12:26.450 --> 00:12:28.870
No!

00:12:30.540 --> 00:12:32.370
--Hey!
--Are you okay?

00:12:32.370 --> 00:12:33.500
I-Is she alive?

00:12:33.500 --> 00:12:36.000
Stop! I don't think she's dead.

00:12:36.000 --> 00:12:39.330
Anyway... Call the ambulance!

00:12:39.330 --> 00:12:43.160
I wonder when they'll notice me...

00:12:43.160 --> 00:12:44.830
No!

00:12:44.830 --> 00:12:47.290
What is this? Who the hell are you guys?

00:12:47.290 --> 00:12:49.290
Hey, stop! Don't touch me!

00:12:49.290 --> 00:12:51.950
--That's my cue for the UFO sound effects.
--Those are my genitals, excuse you!

00:12:53.500 --> 00:12:56.450
The shame we feel around genitals
is impossible to understand?

00:12:56.450 --> 00:12:58.700
How am I supposed to know
the norms of your planet?

00:12:58.700 --> 00:13:01.120
Ah... Hey, wait a minute.

00:13:01.120 --> 00:13:03.000
What's happening right now?

00:13:03.000 --> 00:13:05.160
Their thoughts are penetrating my brain!

00:13:05.160 --> 00:13:05.540
--What? An ambassador?
As in Ambassador Magma?

00:13:05.540 --> 00:13:08.700
--Get outta here.
--What? An ambassador?
As in Ambassador Magma?

00:13:08.700 --> 00:13:09.790
Me?!

00:13:09.790 --> 00:13:13.910
Ah... The fate of invaders who try
to conquer earth with military power

00:13:13.910 --> 00:13:17.500
is told through various video
recordings found on earth?

00:13:17.500 --> 00:13:19.580
Ah, hence the ambassador.

00:13:19.580 --> 00:13:21.540
And where did you find those recordings?

00:13:21.540 --> 00:13:25.080
Are you sure it wasn't a Hollywood movie?
Or Japan's Ultraman?

00:13:25.080 --> 00:13:30.040
A movie! Mo-vie! What is that?
Ugh, it's hard to explain, dammit.

00:13:30.040 --> 00:13:33.790
Whoa! What's this mound?
Is this supposed to be food?

00:13:33.790 --> 00:13:36.540
It only looks like
the Mont-Saint-Michel Abbey to me.

00:13:36.540 --> 00:13:38.660
This is all for me? Seriously?

00:13:38.660 --> 00:13:42.620
Your planet's finest palace cuisine served
to welcome guests? Well, that's an honor.

00:13:42.620 --> 00:13:46.120
But this is too much. Even Rascal Arai
wouldn't be able to handle it.

00:13:46.120 --> 00:13:48.290
Rascal Arai is a competitive eater from Japan.

00:13:48.290 --> 00:13:49.080
--What's a competitive eater? Oh, come on.

00:13:49.080 --> 00:13:50.660
--Look at her face.
--What's a competitive eater? Oh, come on.

00:13:50.660 --> 00:13:54.410
What do you expect me to do when you
confine me fully nude and force me to eat?

00:13:54.410 --> 00:13:57.870
Ah... Wait, what's going on here?

00:13:57.870 --> 00:14:01.250
Mitsuo?! Why are you here?

00:14:01.250 --> 00:14:03.290
And... you're alive...?

00:14:03.290 --> 00:14:06.450
Hey... The stab wound is healed...

00:14:06.450 --> 00:14:09.330
You cloned him? From the blood on my clothes?!

00:14:09.330 --> 00:14:12.200
So I don't go crazy from loneliness?

00:14:12.200 --> 00:14:17.160
All right... So, the feeling
of loneliness is universal.

00:14:17.160 --> 00:14:23.250
But they couldn't figure out
why his blood was on my clothes.

00:14:23.250 --> 00:14:24.660
Thirty seconds left.

00:14:24.660 --> 00:14:26.700
You can't restore his memory?

00:14:26.700 --> 00:14:29.450
That's understandable, you only had his blood.

00:14:29.450 --> 00:14:32.120
Plus, it's probably better that way.

00:14:32.120 --> 00:14:37.540
Huh? What? Who's Mitsuo?
Mitsuo... That's your name.

00:14:37.540 --> 00:14:41.790
You're hungry...? Oh, I bet you are.

00:14:41.790 --> 00:14:44.410
You always get me like that, Mitsuo.

00:14:44.410 --> 00:14:46.750
Let's eat this together.

00:14:46.750 --> 00:14:49.830
There's no way I could eat it all myself.

00:14:56.200 --> 00:14:59.040
Phew...

00:14:59.040 --> 00:15:01.500
Brava.

00:15:01.500 --> 00:15:03.700
That was worthy of some praise.

00:15:03.700 --> 00:15:08.950
That was the third time
I've spoken in the booth...

00:15:08.950 --> 00:15:11.750
But today I felt the most "in the zone."

00:15:11.750 --> 00:15:13.330
What zone?

00:15:13.330 --> 00:15:15.620
Your guess is as good as mine.

00:15:15.620 --> 00:15:20.700
Anyway, I noticed you like to have
punch lines in your story.

00:15:20.700 --> 00:15:22.910
I was impressed. Really.

00:15:22.910 --> 00:15:27.080
Thanks Mr. Mato. So, could you please
do something about this beforehand?

00:15:27.080 --> 00:15:29.750
"*Fill the rest in with whatever you want.
I'm tired. I'm going to sleep."
It's all ad-lib after the aliens appear!

00:15:29.750 --> 00:15:31.750
"*Fill the rest in with whatever you want.
I'm tired. I'm going to sleep."
Does Mr. Kureko hate me or something?

00:15:31.750 --> 00:15:35.750
And why did a UFO get me instead of the cops?

00:15:35.750 --> 00:15:37.950
He said it's a homage to
"The War of the Worlds."

00:15:37.950 --> 00:15:41.200
And he relied on an amateur to come up
with the punch line, to hell with that!

00:15:41.200 --> 00:15:43.660
Apologize to Orson Welles!

00:15:44.620 --> 00:15:49.080
Ah... Well at least I feel
a lot better after that.

00:15:49.080 --> 00:15:50.200
Glad to hear that.

00:15:50.200 --> 00:15:51.330
Oh, huh?

00:15:51.330 --> 00:15:54.750
You were in low spirits when you showed up.

00:15:54.750 --> 00:15:56.580
So that's a relief.

00:15:59.580 --> 00:16:03.620
Mr. Mato... Could I ask you one last favor?

00:16:03.620 --> 00:16:05.370
Huh? What is it?

00:16:07.450 --> 00:16:10.000
Um...

00:16:10.000 --> 00:16:14.660
Could I bill the taxi fee
getting here as an expense?

00:16:14.660 --> 00:16:15.790
That's fine.

00:16:15.790 --> 00:16:20.200
And thank you very much for today.

00:16:22.040 --> 00:16:24.750
Yeah... Likewise.

00:16:24.750 --> 00:16:28.000
And please give us a ride back home!

00:16:28.000 --> 00:16:32.620
Any other "last favors"? I was going
to give you guys a ride anyway.

00:16:33.500 --> 00:16:38.540
There's no time left to negotiate.
We must return home now.

00:16:38.540 --> 00:16:40.750
We're taking this male's blood.

00:16:40.750 --> 00:16:44.660
By acquiring an Earthling's clone,
it'll finally be complete.

00:16:44.660 --> 00:16:47.620
Our Ultra Galactic Super Farm.

00:16:47.620 --> 00:16:49.160
Mitsuo!

00:16:49.160 --> 00:16:51.870
Dammit, aliens with your crazy farm scheme.

00:16:51.870 --> 00:16:55.450
Humans aren't livestock! Take my blood instead!

00:16:55.450 --> 00:16:58.910
I'm used to giving blood. As
long as it's around 400ml.

00:16:58.910 --> 00:17:00.500
See? I have a blood donation card!

00:17:00.500 --> 00:17:08.290
Nice try. It's regulated that women can only
donate 400ml of blood in 16-week intervals.

00:17:08.290 --> 00:17:11.370
--We scanned that card but it's only been
13 weeks since your last donation.

00:17:11.370 --> 00:17:12.370
--What?
--We scanned that card but it's only been
13 weeks since your last donation.

00:17:12.370 --> 00:17:15.410
They're well-informed and oddly considerate.

00:17:15.410 --> 00:17:17.330
While they point a knife to his neck!

00:17:17.330 --> 00:17:20.660
Don't worry about me. I expect
to die every time I wake up.

00:17:20.660 --> 00:17:23.580
Well, if you say so.

00:17:23.580 --> 00:17:24.410
--Huh? What is this?

00:17:24.410 --> 00:17:27.200
--It's our planet's blood collection machine.
--Huh? What is this?

00:17:27.200 --> 00:17:29.370
Ah! It's really gross!

00:17:29.370 --> 00:17:32.830
It's set to collect nutrients so that
your body won't be burdened.

00:17:32.830 --> 00:17:34.660
--Keep living for me, Mitsuo!

00:17:34.660 --> 00:17:36.620
--Chill out, you're not going to die.
--Keep living for me, Mitsuo!

00:17:36.620 --> 00:17:39.200
And save Earth!

00:17:39.200 --> 00:17:41.250
Oh. Miss Minare, you're up.

00:17:41.250 --> 00:17:44.500
Agh... I taste something
really grassy in my mouth...

00:17:44.500 --> 00:17:46.540
Ah! I'm sorry.

00:17:46.540 --> 00:17:49.620
I was changing the water
in the tank since it's my day off.

00:17:49.620 --> 00:17:51.450
You have to stay in here.

00:17:55.500 --> 00:17:58.040
I had the most ridiculous dream ever.

00:17:58.040 --> 00:18:02.000
Of course you'd dream about
aliens after that broadcast.

00:18:02.000 --> 00:18:04.290
Oh... It's not about that.

00:18:04.290 --> 00:18:08.500
Why did I sacrifice myself
to save Mitsuo's life?

00:18:08.500 --> 00:18:11.040
I'll shoot him down from afar.

00:18:11.040 --> 00:18:13.160
Miss Minare, let's take a look.

00:18:13.160 --> 00:18:14.750
Huh?

00:18:14.750 --> 00:18:15.330
There.

00:18:15.330 --> 00:18:17.250
"Radio broadcast gaffe"
"within 24 hours"
Oh... Seriously?

00:18:17.700 --> 00:18:19.750
I don't have to look at that.

00:18:19.750 --> 00:18:21.950
It's only been five hours.

00:18:21.950 --> 00:18:25.000
Who would post things like that
on Sunday morning?

00:18:25.000 --> 00:18:26.120
"Pringle Guy
How freaky..."

00:18:26.120 --> 00:18:27.370
"I know it's late but if anyone's reading
my blog right now, turn the radio on."

00:18:29.620 --> 00:18:30.830
"589: Anonymous @ ON AIR
I checked the MRS homepage
but it's not on the schedule."

00:18:31.040 --> 00:18:32.370
"593: Anonymous @ON AIR
This thread is way too long,
like three days' worth of posts!"

00:18:32.700 --> 00:18:34.830
People noticed quite a bit, huh?

00:18:34.830 --> 00:18:37.040
I'm the one who uploaded the recording
on the video-sharing site

00:18:37.040 --> 00:18:39.750
and posted the link on that thread I started.

00:18:39.750 --> 00:18:41.500
That's what I figured.

00:18:41.500 --> 00:18:43.290
How was the BBS?

00:18:43.290 --> 00:18:45.620
We got about ten inquiries.

00:18:45.620 --> 00:18:48.700
Four of them were seriously concerned
that we were hijacked.

00:18:48.700 --> 00:18:51.500
Can't blame them. It's not on the schedule.

00:18:52.500 --> 00:18:58.410
Minare looked at the script and said,
"Does Mr. Kureko hate me?"

00:18:58.410 --> 00:19:02.250
Give me a break.
Not that I like her or anything.

00:19:02.250 --> 00:19:05.580
You're the one who requested that
the script to be left as open as possible

00:19:05.580 --> 00:19:07.790
so that she'd be forced
to improvise for most of it.

00:19:07.790 --> 00:19:10.910
Yeah, I know. I'll follow up
with her on that later.

00:19:10.910 --> 00:19:14.540
Whatever, it really doesn't matter to me.

00:19:14.540 --> 00:19:16.540
Well, aren't you guys close?

00:19:16.540 --> 00:19:19.200
Chishiro, I want you to listen
to this when you get a chance.

00:19:19.200 --> 00:19:20.540
What is it?

00:19:20.540 --> 00:19:23.620
It's the first episode of Minare Koda's program.

00:19:23.620 --> 00:19:27.080
Oh? Ah, that girl from the curry restaurant.

00:19:27.080 --> 00:19:30.540
Oh, wasn't she fired from that place?

00:19:30.540 --> 00:19:35.000
She was able to keep that job for now,
but she was kicked out of her apartment.

00:19:35.000 --> 00:19:37.540
She's actually staying with Nanba right now.

00:19:37.540 --> 00:19:40.250
I see.

00:19:40.250 --> 00:19:42.830
This was from yesterday? What time did it air?

00:19:42.830 --> 00:19:44.660
Three thirty AM in the morning.

00:19:44.660 --> 00:19:48.830
It's impressive that you found
a sponsor for a C-block program.

00:19:48.830 --> 00:19:55.040
"C-block=Cheapest"
The "C-block" is the late night to early morning
time frame when the ads are cheapest.

00:19:55.040 --> 00:19:58.700
Actually, they're letting us
do it without a sponsor.

00:19:58.700 --> 00:20:01.330
Oh, I see.

00:20:01.330 --> 00:20:03.290
Mr. Mato.

00:20:03.290 --> 00:20:06.580
Don't tell me you're putting her
on Valentine Radio.

00:20:06.580 --> 00:20:08.000
Of course not.

00:20:08.000 --> 00:20:11.080
This woman was an amateur until last night.

00:20:11.080 --> 00:20:12.830
Right.

00:20:12.830 --> 00:20:18.620
My life hasn't changed just because
I talked for 20 minutes on the radio.

00:20:18.620 --> 00:20:23.200
Agh. Would've been nice if I could've lazed
around drinking with Mizuho tonight.

00:20:23.200 --> 00:20:26.120
It sucks that our days off don't match up.

00:20:26.120 --> 00:20:30.620
Dammit. Doing radio until 4 AM then going
to the restaurant at 10 AM is pretty rough.

00:20:30.620 --> 00:20:32.290
Ah, I'm so sleepy.

00:20:32.290 --> 00:20:33.580
May I take your drink orders?

00:20:33.580 --> 00:20:34.950
Hear that? It's her voice.

00:20:34.950 --> 00:20:35.830
Huh?

00:20:35.830 --> 00:20:39.450
Were you on a radio drama late last night?

00:20:39.450 --> 00:20:40.370
Excuse me?

00:20:40.370 --> 00:20:43.580
I was playing mahjong
with these guys late last night.

00:20:43.580 --> 00:20:47.160
It was past 3 AM and we still had the radio on.

00:20:47.160 --> 00:20:50.410
Then out of the blue, during the music program,
I heard a woman's voice saying,

00:20:50.410 --> 00:20:52.660
"I just killed someone" or something.

00:20:52.660 --> 00:20:56.540
It wasn't listed on the schedule,
so we got all excited.

00:20:56.540 --> 00:21:00.580
Then this guy says that voice sounds like the
lady who works at his favorite curry restaurant.

00:21:00.580 --> 00:21:03.160
This guy has a crush on you, by the way.

00:21:03.160 --> 00:21:04.330
Hey! Shut up!

00:21:04.330 --> 00:21:05.750
Well... Actually...

00:21:05.750 --> 00:21:08.330
Seriously? That's awesome.
Does it air every week?

00:21:08.330 --> 00:21:12.750
If Mr. Takarada heard this exchange,
he'd be pissed.

00:21:12.750 --> 00:21:19.290
Anyway, since I never really was interested
before, I didn't realize this until now...

00:21:19.290 --> 00:21:24.250
But I guess there are people who
still listen to the radio these days...

00:21:24.250 --> 00:21:28.790
Miss Minare! Your radio program started already?
You could've told us!

00:21:28.790 --> 00:21:33.080
I didn't mean to hide it.
Plus, it was pretty last minute.

00:21:33.080 --> 00:21:36.500
Besides, you're the one
who kept calling it risky business!

00:21:36.500 --> 00:21:38.330
Well, yes, that's true.

00:21:38.330 --> 00:21:41.910
--Risky business?
--But even then, of course I'd want to listen!

00:21:45.620 --> 00:21:50.290
Even if I had called and told you
about it right before it aired,

00:21:50.290 --> 00:21:52.370
would you have had time to really listen to it?

00:21:52.370 --> 00:21:55.080
What?! What do you want me to say?

00:21:55.080 --> 00:21:56.250
Too obvious of a reaction.

00:21:56.250 --> 00:21:59.250
"Guilty"
Too obvious of a reaction.

00:21:59.250 --> 00:22:01.580
So here's the thing.

00:22:03.120 --> 00:22:07.370
I'm going to move on from curry
and devote myself to radio.

00:22:07.370 --> 00:22:09.910
I might change my mind tomorrow.

00:22:09.910 --> 00:22:12.750
But I'm going to aim to be
Hokkaido's top radio DJ!

00:22:12.750 --> 00:22:16.080
I don't care if I drive away all the men.

00:22:16.080 --> 00:22:17.790
Miss Minare...

00:22:20.750 --> 00:22:22.330
Where are you going?

00:23:44.040 --> 00:23:44.910
"Next Episode"

00:23:44.910 --> 00:23:47.040
"Next Episode"
It all started with a fax we received one day.

00:23:47.040 --> 00:23:49.330
"Preview"
Please help. I'm cursed.

00:23:49.330 --> 00:23:53.790
"Preview"
What did I say? We attract the weirdos
if we keep airing missiles.

00:23:53.790 --> 00:23:58.580
"Preview"
Minare, Nanba. Go visit the sender and record
the investigation from start to finish.

00:23:58.580 --> 00:24:00.580
"Preview"
--What?
--The two of us?

00:24:00.580 --> 00:24:05.580
"Preview"
Mr. Mato, you deserve to contract
an unknown STD and die, seriously.

00:24:05.580 --> 00:24:09.450
"Preview"
Well... It smells fishy, if you ask me.

00:24:09.450 --> 00:24:10.830
"Preview"
The smell of death lingers in
the next episode of <i>Wave, Listen to Me!</i>:

00:24:10.830 --> 00:24:12.080
The smell of death lingers in
the next episode of <i>Wave, Listen to Me!</i>:

00:24:12.080 --> 00:24:14.080
"There's No Such Thing."

00:24:14.080 --> 00:24:17.040
"See you next time!"
"Illustrated by Hiroaki Samura"
